          %h2#on_locally_compact_hausdorff_topological_spaces On locally compact Hausdorff topological spaces
          %p Radon measures on locally compact Hausdorff topological spaces admit yet another, Daniell-style definition, which is explored in detail in Bourbaki’s book.
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a locally compact Hausdorff topological space. A
              %strong Radon measure
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a positive linear functional
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi R
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu\colon C_c(X,\mathbf{R})\to\mathbf{R},
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_c
              refers to the vector space of continuous compactly supported functions.
          %p
            Such
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            induces a pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (m,M)
            in the sense of above definitions as follows:
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi μ
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M=\mu^*
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi μ
                      %mover
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m=\mu^{\bar*}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi μ
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu^*
            is the outer measure associated to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi μ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi inf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊃
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi is
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Borel
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu^*(A)=\inf\{\mu(\chi_B)\mid B\supset A,\; B\; is\; Borel\}
          %p
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi μ
                    %mover
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu^{\bar*}
            is the essential measure associated to
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi μ
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu^*
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi μ
                    %mover
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi sup
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi μ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi μ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi is
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi finite
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu^{\bar*}(A)=\sup\{\mu^*(C)\mid C\subset A,\; \mu^*(C)\; is\; finite\}.
          %p
            (For σ-finite spaces we have
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi μ
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi μ
                      %mover
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu^*=\mu^{\bar*}
          %p
            Vice versa, given
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            as the integral with respect to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
          %h2#pushforwards_of_radon_measures Pushforwards of Radon measures
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+spaces"} Hausdorff topological spaces
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi m
                    %mo ,
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu=(m,M)
              is a Radon measure on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H\colon X\to Y
              is
              %strong
                Lusin
                = succeed "-measurable" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
              if for any compact
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K\subset X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon\gt0
              there is a compact
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K'\subset K
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi K
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(K\setminus K')\lt\epsilon
              and the restriction of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K'
              is continuous. We say that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              is
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
                \-proper
              if, in addition, every point of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              has a neighborhood whose inverse image is
              = succeed "-integrable." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
          %p
            For example, continuous maps are Lusin
            = succeed "-measurable" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
          %p
            Lusin
            = succeed "-measurable" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            with respect to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Any Lusin
            = succeed "-measurable" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            = succeed "-measurable" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            = succeed "-measurable" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metrizable"} metrizable
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable"} separable
            = succeed "-measurable" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            = succeed "-measurable." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
          %p
            Step functions and lower semicontinuous maps are always Lusin
            = succeed "-measurable." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H\colon X\to Y
              is a
              = succeed "-proper" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo *
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_*\mu
              is a Radon measure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              defined as follows. Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+subset"} Borel subset
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\subset Y
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo *
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi μ
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_*\mu(B)=\mu^\bullet(H^*(B)).
            %p
              This yields a Radon measure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H\colon X\to Y
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+spaces"} Hausdorff topological spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              is the pushforward along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              of a Radon measure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
              is concentrated in a countable union of images under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              of compact subsets of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If a Radon measure is
                = succeed "-finite" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %li
              %p
                A Radon measure on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CF%84-additive"} τ-additive
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+space"} compact Hausdorff space
            %li
              %p
                Radon
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+measures"} probability measures
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact Hausdorff spaces
                form a
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Radon+monad"} Radon monad
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+metric+spaces"} complete metric spaces
                give the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kantorovich+monad"} Kantorovich monad
          %p
            (See also
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads+of+probability%2C+measures+and+valuations"} monads of probability, measures and valuations
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            Most measures of interest in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            are Radon. For example
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+measures"} Dirac measures
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lebesgue+measure"} Lebesgue measure
                on the real line.
            %li
              %p
                The measure associated to a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+form"} volume form
                on a Riemannian manifold.
            %li
              %p
                The left (right)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haar+measure"} Haar measure
                on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+group"} locally compact topological group
                is a nonzero Radon measure which is invariant under left (right) multiplications by elements in the group.
          %h2#see_also See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Radon+monad"}> Radon monad
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kantorovich+monad"} Kantorovich monad
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads+of+probability%2C+measures%2C+and+valuations"} monads of probability, measures, and valuations
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+measure"}> Borel measure
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CF%84-additive+measure"} τ-additive measure
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+valuation"} continuous valuation
          %h2#references References
          %p The canonical references on Radon measures are
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laurent+Schwartz"}> Laurent Schwartz
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Radon measures on arbitrary topological spaces and cylindrical measures
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Bourbaki"}> Nicolas Bourbaki
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Integration. Chapter IX
          %p More recent expositions include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                V. Bogachev,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Measure Theory
